          "title": "You'll want to know: آنگاه",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "آنگاه (ângâh) — \"then, at that point\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "شام خوردیم و آنگاه به پارک رفتیم. Shâm khordim va ângâh be pârk raftim. We had dinner and then went to the park."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Literary; in speech ba'd. In writing it can answer an agar clause: \"if..., then...\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ângâh is built from Persian ân \"that\" and gâh \"time, place\", both native words: \"that time\"."
            }
          ]
        },
