          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "در نهایت (dar nahâyat) — \"ultimately, in the end\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "در نهایت (dar nahâyat) تصمیم گرفتیم در خانه بمانیم. Dar nahâyat tasmim gereftim dar khâne bemânim. Ultimately we decided to stay at home."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "nahâyat alone means \"the utmost\": nahâyat-e lotf \"the height of kindness\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "nahâyat is borrowed from Arabic nihāya, \"end, limit\" (EtymDB lists the Arabic source); dar \"in\" is inherited Persian."
            }
          ]
        },
